# Sign-ins and saved secrets (Identity and Credentials)
error-cred-admin-consent-required = Your organisation has to approve ordin before you can sign in with Microsoft. Ask whoever manages your Microsoft 365, or use a company profile.
error-cred-ambiguous = You have more than one sign-in saved for this. Choose which one to use.
error-cred-browser-failed = ordin couldn't open your web browser. Open it yourself and try again.
error-cred-certificate-expired = That certificate has expired. Choose one that is still valid.
error-cred-certificate-invalid = That certificate and key can't be used. Check that both files are present and belong together.
error-cred-challenge-unknown = That sign-in attempt isn't recognised. Start signing in again.
error-cred-config-invalid = The settings for how ordin keeps secrets don't suit this set-up. Check them and try again.
error-cred-duplicate = You already have a sign-in saved with that name for this service. Choose a different name.
error-cred-flow-not-offered = That way of signing in isn't available here. Choose another way.
error-cred-keychain-missing = Your saved sign-in has gone missing from this computer. Sign in again.
error-cred-keychain-unavailable = ordin can't reach your saved sign-ins on this computer. Unlock it and try again.
error-cred-kind-has-no-token = This kind of sign-in uses a password, so it has no access code to give.
error-cred-kind-mismatch = This sign-in doesn't use a password. Use the matching kind of sign-in.
error-cred-label-invalid = The account name is too short or too long. Choose another.
error-cred-loopback-busy = ordin couldn't finish signing in because the connection it needs is busy. Close other programs and try again.
error-cred-not-found = That sign-in couldn't be found. It may have been removed.
error-cred-password-invalid = The password is empty or too long. Enter a password up to 1,024 characters.
error-cred-provider-not-configured = Signing in to that service isn't set up in this version of ordin.
error-cred-provider-refused = The service refused the sign-in. Check the details and try again.
error-cred-provider-unreachable = ordin couldn't reach that service. Check your internet connection and try again.
error-cred-refresh-refused = The service no longer accepts your sign-in. Sign in again.
error-cred-relay-state-mismatch = That sign-in doesn't match the one you started, so it was refused. Start signing in again.
error-cred-scope-missing = Your sign-in doesn't allow what ordin needs. Sign in again and approve every permission it asks for.
error-cred-secret-in-record = A password or secret was found where it shouldn't be saved, so it was not kept.
error-cred-secret-key-conflict = Two different secret keys are set up. Keep only one and try again.
error-cred-secret-key-exists = A secret key file already exists there. Choose a different place.
error-cred-secret-key-invalid = That secret key isn't valid. Copy it again exactly as you were given it.
error-cred-secret-key-missing = No secret key is set up for saving secrets. Set one up and try again.
error-cred-secret-name-invalid = That secret name isn't allowed. Use only the letters, digits and symbols the form accepts.
error-cred-secret-store-absent = Saved secrets aren't available in this setup.
error-cred-secret-store-corrupt = Your saved secrets file can't be read. It may be damaged or from a different version.
error-cred-secret-store-write-failed = ordin couldn't save your secrets file. Check there is free space and try again.
error-cred-secret-too-large = That secret is too large. Keep it under 64 KiB.
error-cred-sign-in-cancelled = Signing in was cancelled. Try again when you're ready.
error-cred-sign-in-required = You need to sign in again to carry on.
error-cred-sign-in-timeout = Signing in took too long and stopped. Try again.
error-cred-store-failed = ordin couldn't save your sign-in. Try again.
error-cred-systemd-creds-failed = ordin couldn't unlock or create the key that protects your saved secrets on this computer. Try again.
error-cred-too-many-sign-ins = Too many sign-ins are waiting. Finish or cancel one, then try again.
error-cred-url-invalid = The web address must start with https and be reasonably short. Check it and try again.
